## Summary

The syntax highlighter (shAll) re-matched the class=sh-* attributes it injects, corrupting the generated span tags and rendering literal text such as class=sh-str inside code blocks (most visible in PHP snippets).

## Changes

- Keyword regex now uses a negative lookahead (?![=]) so it skips the class attribute of injected spans.
- HTML attribute regex now excludes class via (?!class).

Both changes are in mdview.c (build_js / shAll). Verified with a Node replay of the highlighter against the reported PHP sample - strings, keywords and function calls highlight correctly with no leaked/escaped span tags.

