## V1.0.7 — European Primary Nutrition Policy

Implements the explicitly approved Canary/Spain/Europe nutrition-source policy on top of the completed B4 corroboration lane.

### Source selection
- selects source **per ingredient and per tracked nutrient**;
- prefers reviewed ANSES-Ciqual evidence when food-form match is equally good or better and the Ciqual constituent confidence is A/B/C;
- Ciqual D-confidence fields do not displace an available USDA field;
- stronger USDA food-form matches remain primary;
- a reviewed Ciqual field may be used when USDA has no reviewed value, with exact provenance retained;
- no cross-source averaging.

### Semantic firewall
- USDA carbohydrate-by-difference (`1005`) and Ciqual available carbohydrate (`CHOAVL`) remain distinct;
- a recipe that would require summing both semantics fails that nutrient closed rather than manufacturing one carbohydrate total;
- EU 1169/2011 Ciqual energy is used when Ciqual is selected for European context;
- all selected fields retain source, identifier, method, semantic, match confidence, Ciqual field confidence and selection reason.

### Runtime
- `publicNutritionSource` now calculates against the deterministic European-primary selected density map;
- partial/incompatible coverage still preserves the project-authored estimate;
- complete coverage exposes the source policy and per-nutrient provenance;
- existing USDA evidence-backed quantity conversion rules remain unchanged;
- recommendation ranking, hard constraints, shell semantics and medical/allergy boundaries are unchanged.

### Tests
Adds explicit policy tests for European preference, stronger-USDA retention, Ciqual-only evidence, no averaging, mixed-carbohydrate fail-closed behavior and deterministic coverage.

No runtime API, backend, paid service, larger runner, runtime LLM or private Knowledge Core dependency. Culinary & Nutrition Brain remains NOT AUTHORIZED.

